# PATTERN 1: FUNCTION CHAINING
# Start the app (F5). Visual Studio starts Azurite for you. Then click "Send request" above each call.
# Watch the console: Enrich fails ~30% of the time, and you'll see the retry policy kick in.

# URL and keys come from http-client.env.json. Local values are the default; to test the deployed app, choose azure at the top right of this editor.

### Happy path: Validate → Enrich → Score → Persist
# @name submitLoan
POST {{baseUrl}}/loans
x-functions-key: {{functionKey}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "id": "loan-1001",
  "applicantId": "alice",
  "amount": 25000
}

### Check the result (reuses StatusQueryGetUri from the response above)
# If your editor doesn't support request variables, paste the StatusQueryGetUri here instead.
GET {{submitLoan.response.body.$.StatusQueryGetUri}}

### Validation failure: not retried, so it goes straight to compensation → output "ManualReview"
POST {{baseUrl}}/loans
x-functions-key: {{functionKey}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "id": "loan-1002",
  "applicantId": "bob",
  "amount": -5
}
